// DRAFT (Act III, planning only). Ch19 I04 "The words" (optional, E, 2 min, ~100 words). act3_ch19.md §2 I04;
// act3_threads T-04; ending_cost_audit §6. Ysolde and Asha on the plaza steps. Ysolde has the Eighth Verse whole (the
// words from the Choir stones, the tune read through the farewell-tide, its place from Ama's question-knot). She reads
// the words aloud, SPOKEN, NOT SUNG (README rule 3); Asha repeats them once, spoken. Then Ysolde's want turns, dry,
// never a joke. THE WORDS ARE AUDIO'S (docs/kb/audio/lamptongue.md §2 verse 8, §3): Ysolde reads verse 8 whole as cut in
// the stones; Asha repeats only its first line and its last word (she doesn't have the rest by heart yet).
title: ch19_the_words
location: prologue
---
@camera I04
@mark ysolde plaza_steps_b walk
@anim ysolde open book
@wait 2.0
Ysolde [neutral]: Ish oan, ish oan. Vey hal, ennu tash. Oan re, oan re... tash. #line:ch19_words_001 #lamptongue #notr #tn:"Lamptongue, the Eighth Verse as cut in the stones (lamptongue.md verse 8): keep exactly as written. Spoken flat, not sung."
@wait 2.0
Asha [neutral]: Ish oan, ish oan... tash. #line:ch19_words_002 #lamptongue #notr #tn:"Lamptongue: keep exactly as written. Asha repeats only the first line and the last word, spoken."
@wait 2.0
Ysolde [neutral]: Never the words and the tune together. Not until it's time. #line:ch19_words_003
@anim ysolde close book
@wait 3.0
Ysolde [neutral]: I came to give you a good death. #line:ch19_words_004
@wait 2.0
Ysolde [tender]: I would like to give you a long, dull life instead. #line:ch19_words_005
@wait 2.0
Asha [soft_smile]: I'll try. #line:ch19_words_007
<<set $ch19_words_whole = true>>
===
